From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] sal: allow the source directory in log locations to be set

SAL_INFO and SAL_WARN locations are __FILE__, and sal shortens them by
the source directory compiled in as SRCDIR. A distribution build maps
__FILE__ to where it installs the sources for debugging
(-ffile-prefix-map), so the build directory in SRCDIR no longer
shortens anything, and it is left in libuno_sal.so, where the
OpenEmbedded buildpaths check finds it.

Take SAL_LOG_SRCDIR instead when it is set, so such a build can name
the mapped directory; SRCDIR stays the default.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff --git a/sal/Library_sal.mk b/sal/Library_sal.mk
--- a/sal/Library_sal.mk
+++ b/sal/Library_sal.mk
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@
 	-DSAL_DLLIMPLEMENTATION \
 	-DRTL_OS="\"$(RTL_OS)\"" \
 	-DRTL_ARCH="\"$(RTL_ARCH)\"" \
-	-DSRCDIR="\"$(SRCDIR)\"" \
+	-DSRCDIR="\"$(or $(SAL_LOG_SRCDIR),$(SRCDIR))\"" \
     $(call gb_CondLibSalTextenc,-DCOND_LIB_SAL_TEXTENC) \
 ))
 
